ultivate focus\nAugust 10, 2026\nWriter Carmen Maria Machado on focusing on what interests you\nAugust 6, 2026\nMulti-disciplinary artist Suchitra Mattai on trusting in your art and in your process\nAugust 5, 2026\nWriter and translator Kate Briggs on pursuing your own questions\nAugust 4, 2026\nMusician Jessica Pratt on exploring new territory without losing yourself\nAugust 3, 2026\nEssay:\nThe Language of Artist Statements\nAugust 2, 2026\nArtist, activist, and author Edie Fake on communicating with images\nJuly 31, 2026\nMusician and artist Alexandra Drewchin (Eartheater) on following the deep feeling\nJuly 31, 2026\nArtist and technologist Mindy Seu on needing deadlines\nJuly 30, 2026\nArtist Saif Azzuz on changing all the time\nJuly 29, 2026\nMusician and Radiohead guitarist Ed O'Brien on turning dark times into beautiful things\nJuly 29, 2026\nWriter, publisher and chainmaille artist Naomi Falk on the creative value of transformation\nJuly 28, 2026\nMusician and producer Rostam on friendship and collaboration\nJuly 27, 2026\nMusicians feeble little horse on knowing when it’s right\nJuly 27, 2026\nHerbalist and author Rachelle Robinett on rebalancing how you work and live\nJuly 24, 2026\nActor, writer, and streamer Felicia Day on having something to prove\nJuly 23, 2026\nArtist and filmmaker Glenn Kaino on starting with belief\nJuly 23, 2026\nMusician Charlotte Day Wilson on finding greatness\nJuly 22, 2026\nArtist Sara Cwynar on flowing through it\nJuly 21, 2026\nWriter Annakeara Stinson on learning to find clarity in your work\nJuly 20, 2026\nMusicians Mo Chara and Móglaí Bap (Kneecap) on shaking the foundations of the status quo\nJuly 17, 2026\nFilmmaker Jalena Keane-Lee on the power of responsible storytelling\nJuly 16, 2026\nEditor Hillary Brenhouse on emboldening others to take risks\nJuly 15, 2026\nMusician Angelo De Augustine on healing over time\nJuly 14, 2026\nAuthor and anthropologist Ashanté M. Reese on using ritual to connect to your work\nJuly 13